+{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01YDTZiJdc8YnNjsBwtqvn5J","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All three validation gates pass. The document management API is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nBuilt a permission-aware document management API with Express + TypeScript and in-memory storage.\n\n**Files created:**\n- `src/types.ts` — domain types (User, Folder, Document, Share, ActivityLogEntry, Role)\n- `src/store.ts` — in-memory `Store` class (Maps/arrays) with helpers for users, tokens, folders, documents, shares, and activity logging\n- `src/permissions.ts` — the core permission engine\n- `src/app.ts` — `createApp()` returning the Express app with all routes\n- `src/index.ts` — re-exports `createApp` and starts a server when run directly\n- `tests/api.test.ts` — 15 supertest tests (kept out of `src/` so `tsc`/`eslint` stay focused on app code)\n\n**Key design decisions:**\n\n- **Auth:** `POST /auth/register` (+ `/users`) and `POST /auth/login` (+ `/login`) issue opaque bearer tokens; a single middleware gates everything else and returns 401 on missing/invalid tokens.\n\n- **Permission resolution** (`effectiveRole`): collects every role a user is granted on a resource — ownership, direct shares, and shares on the containing folder *and all ancestor folders* — then returns the **most permissive** via rank (`viewer` < `editor` < `owner`). Folder-chain walking guards against cycles.\n\n- **Capability mapping:** viewer→read; editor→read/modify/share; owner→+delete/manage-roles. Creating a child folder or document requires *modify* rights on the parent folder. Editors can share but only owners can grant the `owner` role.\n\n- **Routes:** full CRUD on `/folders` and `/documents` (including nested `POST /folders/:folderId/documents`), share via `POST /folders/:id/share`, `POST /documents/:id/share`, or generic `POST /share`, plus `GET /activity`. Folder deletion recursively removes the subtree and its documents.\n\n- **Activity log** records creation, updates, deletion, and sharing — each with action, user, target resource, and ISO timestamp.\n\nTests cover auth flows, CRUD, role enforcement (viewer/editor/owner boundaries), folder-inheritance, most-permissive resolution across multiple paths, subtree deletion, and activity logging."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":131,"cache_creation_input_tokens":397,"cache_read_input_tokens":38055,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":397},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"18930a72-5b92-4f05-8f34-a6ff2a8dd921","uuid":"c102f598-4e71-4825-acfc-67c5b357de98","request_id":"req_011CbVcki7PrDWeSuojrGtrS"}
